  "body": "Closes #1, #2, #6, #14, #15, #18, #19, #21, #26.\nRefs #4, #16, #17, #20, #22, #27 (partially addressed; the rest needs a decision).\n\nNine commits, one per area. Every claim below was re-verified against a clean\nbuild of bf80156 on this machine, not taken from the report.\n\n## What this fixes\n\n| Issue | Commit | Verified by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| #14 `inject --pidfile` panics after spawning when `getrandom` fails | `inject:` | seccomp launcher denying `getrandom`: rc 134 + orphaned stubs before, rc 0 + a stoppable run after |\n| #1 psgen's own pidfile is refused on the next run | `probe:` | second `inject` against the same path: rc 2 before, rc 0 after; `doctor` DENY before, ALLOW after |\n| #26 a pidfile basename near `NAME_MAX` fails after spawning | `probe:` | 240-byte basename: 2 stubs spawned and rc 1 before, exit 2 before spawning after |\n| #19 `doctor` reports `seccomp_user_notif blocked` on a normal kernel | `probe:` | `EFAULT` from a null filter program: `blocked` before, `reachable` after |\n| seccomp `KILL_PROCESS` kills `psgen` itself | `probe:` | `memfd_create`/`bpf`/`seccomp` kill filter: `doctor` and `inject --dry-run` rc 159 before, rc 0 after |\n| #15 `stop --dry-run` kills the run | `cli:` | `stop --dry-run` -> rc 2, nothing signalled |\n| #2 the same seed is not reproducible a second later | `gen:` | `table -n 20 -s 42` twice, 2 s apart: 32 lines differ before, identical after |\n| #18 postgres workers are session leaders | `gen:` | `inject -f db`: `Ss` with `sid == pid` before, the postmaster's session after |\n| #21 `check --binaries` reports an existing path as missing | `check:` | `/usr/lib/bluetooth/bluetoothd` exists and was reported missing; not after |\n| #6 the test suite aborts on a constrained host | `tests:` | before: `SubprocessError` at the first check; after: `invariants: ok`, `smoke: ok` |\n\n## Partially addressed, on purpose\n\n- **#4** -- the subtree count is fixed (40-row stop: `33/35/34` before, `40/40/40`\n  after, three runs each) and an unreadable live PID now counts as failed instead\n  of skipped. The *zombie* half is not fixed: a `Z` still accepts a signal, and\n  whether `stopped` should exclude it changes what the count means.\n- **#17** -- `--local` now overrides `--utc-offset` (`TZ=Asia/Kolkata`: local+120\n  gave 09:50 before, 07:50 after). The unbounded `--utc-offset` is not fixed.\n- **#16** -- the shortfall is now warned about instead of silent; the padding and\n  the count semantics are untouched.\n- **#22** -- the help now says a one-field line is proc-self only; the form itself\n  is unchanged.\n- **#27** -- `After=sysinit.target` instead of a target that does not exist. The\n  restart itself still depends on #1 (which this closes) and on `ExecStop=-`.\n\n## Not touched, because the fix is a design decision\n\n#20 (proposed patch, **not run as root here** -- treat as a proposal), #23\n`load --mem-util`, #24 `log --lines`, #25 fd 3 config trust, #28 impossible values.\nEach has the trade-offs written down in its issue.\n\n## Notes for review\n\n- This is the QA bundle's combined patch, unmodified in substance, split into\n  commits by area. `git diff main..HEAD` differs from that patch only by the three\n  `tests/invariants.py` hunks for #6 -- added because the bundle's patch alone still\n  aborts the suite on a host with a finite hard `RLIMIT_FSIZE` or no `/dev/ptmx`.\n  That is worth knowing if you were planning to apply the patch as-is.\n- Each commit builds on its own (`cargo build --release` at every step), so it\n  bisects.\n- `cargo clippy --release` reports the same 23 warnings as `bf80156`; this adds\n  none. `cargo fmt --check` still fails, identically before and after -- the hits\n  are pre-existing and in files this does not touch.\n- Two commits change generated output on purpose: `%MEM` now rounds like procps,\n  and postgres rows become children of the postmaster. Both move golden output and\n  both are argued in their issues.\n\nWe aim to provide the software that shapes the world of tomorrow.\n\n---\n\nRequested by Ajam via errand.\nConversation: https://discord.com/channels/1313385177703256064/1569172924408008815\n",
